    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=2,\\ b=-2$.",
      "worked": "The tangent and normal meet at the point of contact:\n$$\\begin{align*}2x-1&=-\\frac12x+\\frac32\\\\x&=1\\\\y&=1.\\end{align*}$$\nThe point $(1,1)$ lies on the curve, so $a+b+1=1$, giving $a+b=0$. The tangent gradient is $2$, and $y'=2ax+b$, so $2a+b=2$. Hence $a=2$ and $b=-2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
